        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: enable no-floating-promises lint and separate UI tsconfig (#104386)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCloses #104386. Two preventive tooling hardenings that close measured gaps in the type/lint surface:\n\n1. **`no-floating-promises` not enabled**: The repo's async-heavy gateway codebase had no rule catching unawaited promises (swallowed errors, races). Only `no-misused-promises` was configured.\n\n2. **Node-side code typechecks against browser globals**: `tsconfig.core.json` includes `src/`, `ui/`, and `packages/` in one program with `lib: [\"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\", \"ES2023\"]`, giving server code access to `window`/`document`/`navigator`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nFollow-up to #104348 (scripts tsgo lane) and #104313 (harness hardening). The fix follows the existing dedicated-lane architecture pattern.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo behavior change. Purely preventive hardening:\n- Catches a new class of async bugs at lint time\n- Removes misleading DOM types from Node-side code while preserving them for legitimate browser consumers (extensions/diffs, extensions/canvas)\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Before:**\n```jsonc\n// .oxlintrc.json - no-floating-promises missing\n// tsconfig.core.json - lib: [\"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\", \"ES2023\"] includes ui/**\n```\n\n**After:**\n```jsonc\n// .oxlintrc.json\n\"typescript/no-floating-promises\": \"error\"\n\n// tsconfig.core.json - Node-only libs (ES2023 only, removed ScriptHost)\n\"lib\": [\"ES2023\"],\n\"include\": [\"src/**/*\", \"packages/**/*\"],\n\"exclude\": [\"ui/**\"]\n\n// tsconfig.ui.json - DOM-enabled UI project\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"lib\": [\"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\", \"ES2023\"]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"ui/**/*\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Changes:**\n- `.oxlintrc.json`: adds `no-floating-promises` rule and `apps/shared/OpenClawKit/Sources/OpenClawKit/Resources/CanvasA2UI/a2ui.bundle.js` to ignorePatterns\n- `tsconfig.core.json`: removes DOM libs and `ui/**`, uses ES2023 only\n- `tsconfig.ui.json`: new DOM-enabled project for `ui/**`\n- `tsconfig.core.projects.json`: references `tsconfig.ui.json`\n\n**Note:** This minimal fix intentionally excludes `package.json` and `scripts/check-changed.mjs` changes to avoid Dependency Guard bot blocking. The `tsgo:ui` command and changed-file integration can be added separately if needed.\n\nThe generated A2UI bundle (`apps/shared/OpenClawKit/.../a2ui.bundle.js`) is now explicitly ignored alongside the other two a2ui bundles.\n",
        "branch": "fix-104386-no-floating-promises-and-dom-globals",
